From da3115632dbb82d30d438b42dd59283e1b29d7d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:06:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 150/162] net: airoha: make GPON session recovery deterministic

Stopping the GPON data netdev currently leaves the optical activation
running.  If LOS or TO2 disables the MAC while optical_active remains set,
a later ndo_open skips sfp_upstream_start() and the ONU stays in O1 until
an unrelated identity update happens to schedule restart_work.

The same recovery path also retains OLT-created OMCI MEs and duplicate
transaction state.  Reusing that stale state after a new GPON activation
can prevent the OLT from completing MIB synchronization.  Meanwhile, the
EN7523 continuously asserts GEM delineation and receive error interrupts
while acquiring downstream framing, which can starve the ordered GPON FSM
workqueue used by PLOAM and restart processing.

Make netdev stop synchronously stop the SFP upstream and GPON MAC, cancel
pending restarts when the interface is administratively down, and restart
the same optical identity after TO2 or a recovered SFP link.  Add a full
OMCI session reset that invalidates the channel, clears queued and
duplicate transactions, removes OLT-origin MEs, and resets MIB
synchronization.

Keep GPON MAC initialization asynchronous with respect to PHY_READY, as the
EN7523 digital PHY may only synchronize after the MAC activation sequence
has started.  Mask the continuously asserted acquisition error sources but
retain their hardware counters and the actionable TX-late interrupt.

Fixes: b4c80ace04c5 ("net: airoha: keep xPON activation alive across netdev cycles")
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
